  "term": "lie scale",
  "definition": "A lie scale is a personality questionnaire measure reflecting a tendency to present oneself in a socially desirable way or to “fake good.” In this source, higher lie-scale scores were associated with greater reported use of smell-related cues in everyday decisions.",
